  "finalRuntimeReplayBasis": "release04 compiled artifacts exactly match directly replayed release02 and core01; added tests/formatting do not alter production.",
  "review": {
    "scope": "Static review of main-authored src/svg-scene.ts production diff against HEAD and read-only inspection of main-authored validation evidence. Not independent review of this worker's test additions.",
    "verdict": "passed_with_nonblocking_accounting_and_complexity_caveats",
    "blockingFindings": [],
    "nonblockingFindings": [
      {
        "id": "accounting-change",
        "locations": [
          "src/svg-scene.ts:318",
          "src/svg-scene.ts:614"
        ],
        "assessment": "This is intentionally not byte-identical accounting. Unexamined trailing IDs no longer contribute lookup source or work. Additionally, an outside-definition descendant ID can now be preflighted before a deferred lookup reaches it: old eager indexing charged its ID to sourceCodeUnits before geometry preflight charged it again; the new order charges the source once during preflight and only work during indexing. A missing nested clip reference can trigger this interleaving in an otherwise successful scene. The requested outside definition's own ID, if indexed before preflight, retains the previous double source contribution. sourceCodeUnits, source-limit admission and error timing can therefore differ even when a later lookup ultimately scans the same nodes. Required geometry and ID contents remain accounted for, and per-ID lookup work is not skipped."
      },
      {
        "id": "existing-node-snapshot-cost",
        "locations": [
          "src/svg-scene.ts:325",
          "src/svg-scene.ts:328",
          "src/document.ts:1084"
        ],
        "assessment": "The generator continuation is O(depth), but that is not a bound on total document-access allocation or CPU. Existing DocumentTree.get() creates and caches immutable copies of a node's complete children array and attributes on a cache miss. Visiting a wide ancestor may therefore copy references to unvisited tail siblings without proportional SVG work charging. This pre-existing API cost is not introduced or fixed by the production diff; do not describe this patch as eliminating all tail-dependent allocation or establishing an end-to-end O(depth) memory bound."
      }
    ],
    "liveApproved": false
  },
